/**
 * @file w_forms_test.cpp
 * @brief The base RV64 W instructions assemble, encode as the spec lays
 *        them out, and execute with 32-bit wrap and sign extension on all
 *        five models (known_issues 109).
 *
 * addw subw sllw srlw sraw addiw slliw srliw sraiw had encodings and both
 * executors decoded them, but instruction_syntax_map had no entry, so the
 * parser rejected every one of them.
 *
 * The tables are generated by ~/atlas-verify/e3/gen_w.py:
 *   kEncoding  each source line with the word an encoder written from the
 *              spec's R/I field layout gives (not the assembler's tables);
 *   kCases     padded programs, operands from a .data table, results in
 *              x12..x31, values from a Python RV64IM oracle. Register shift
 *              counts 0/31/32/63 (masked to 5 bits), immediate shifts 0 and
 *              31, rd = x0, rs1 = rd, and the M-extension W forms and
 *              negw/sext.w as regression cases (those already worked).
 */
